    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0021" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.2221/45a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-20T18:00:00-04:00">January 20, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>105. Radio Chungking has recently quoted a number of reports in the Chinese press
                    in regard to the “growing movement” among Chinese students for enlistment in the
                    Chinese Armed Forces.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d9-f1"/> One report referred to
                    20,000 students having enlisted in recent weeks. In another the opinion was
                    expressed that “the infusion into the army of students will not only strengthen
                    the Chinese Armed Forces but will have a beneficial influence on the internal
                    situation of the country as well”.</p>
                <p>Have you any comments?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d9-f1" n="28" xml:id="d9-f1-content">
                <p>In despatch No. 2018, January 13, the Ambassador in China reported on the “Join
                    the Army Movement” of Chinese students (893.2221/47).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
